# Desk Buddy — Project Intelligence

## Architecture Rules
- Main process (`main.js`) handles tray, IPC, scheduler, screen-share detection — NO DOM/rendering code here
- Renderer process (`renderer/main.js`) owns the Three.js scene, state machine, character orchestration
- All tunables (speeds, heights, character configs) live in `renderer/config.js` — never hardcode values in main.js or characters.js
- New characters: add to `CHARACTERS` array in `main.js` AND `renderer/config.js` AND handle in `createCharacter()` factory in `renderer/characters.js`

## Character System Patterns
- All procedural characters expose `{ object, play(name), poke(), update(dt) }` interface
- `Character` wrapper class adds `.x`, `.face(dir)`, YAW rotation, smooth facing transition
- `YAW = Math.PI / 2 - 0.45` — do NOT change this; it correctly makes the body's +Z face the camera
- **ALL characters must be built in side-profile orientation**: +X = walking direction, +Y = up, +Z = screen depth
  - Face features (eyes, screen, mouth) belong on the `+X` face so YAW presents them to the viewer
  - e.g. CoffeeCup face at `x ≈ +0.38` (cylinder radius), handle at `-X`; TerminalBot CRT screen at `x > 0`
  - Legs run front/rear along X axis; arms/wings splay in ±Z
  - Violating this = character appears sideways or with its back to the viewer
- RoboDog uses **spheres and cylinders only** — no BoxGeometry (per user feedback: "too rectangular")
- Head faces naturally along body +Z — do NOT add `head.rotation.y` override (causes over-rotation)
- `MeshPhongMaterial` (`meshP()`) for RoboDog/TerminalBot/CoffeeCup; `MeshLambertMaterial` (`mat()`) for animals
- Animations: time-based sinusoidal curves in `update(dt)` — no Three.js AnimationMixer for procedural chars
- Character switching: `onCharacterSet` must NOT guard with `if (active) return` — switching mid-animation re-enters `walkIn` with new character immediately

## Screen-Share Detection Rules
- ONLY pause when user is **actively in a meeting** — not just because the app is open
- `CptHost.exe` = reliable Zoom share signal (only present during active screen share)
- Teams: use PowerShell mic-in-use registry check, NOT process count heuristics
- OBS is always broadcasting when running → safe to pause
- Never use `teams.exe` presence alone as a signal (too many false positives)

## User Preferences
- Character should be **tall enough to see** — RoboDog height = 240px
- Face should be **straight toward the screen** — achieved via YAW, no extra rotation
- Animation should feel alive: wagging tail, breathing, head sway even in idle
- Tail wag should cascade through segments (phase delay between seg1/2/3)

## Files NOT to commit
- `test-app.js` — one-off electron import debug script
- `version` — auto-generated by electron tooling
- `electron-*.zip` — binary archives, gitignored

## Testing
- `npm test` runs `test/scheduler.test.js` via `node:test` — no extra deps needed
- Scheduler tests require NO GUI/Electron — pure Node.js

## Desk Assistant Architecture
- `renderer/aideClient.js` — ESM fetch-based SSE streaming client (port of aideClient.ts, no TS)
- `preload-assistant.cjs` — contextBridge exposing only `getCredentials()` and `close()` to assistant window
- `renderer/assistant.html` + `renderer/assistant.js` — standalone BrowserWindow, NOT part of the overlay
- Assistant window uses `sandbox: false` so Web Speech API + fetch work directly in renderer
- AiDE credentials live in `~/.aide_creds/.env` (keys: `AIDE_BASE_URL`, `AIDE_TOKEN`)
- Credentials loaded at startup via `loadAideCredentials()` in main.js; lazy retry on first IPC call
- Streaming: main process streams AiDE SSE via Node.js `fetch` and relays tokens to renderer via IPC (`assistant:token`, `assistant:done`, `assistant:error`) — do NOT fetch SSE from the renderer (Chromium `chunked_data_pipe` ERR_FAILED)
- TTS: `SpeechSynthesis` split by sentences for low-latency first word; Stop button calls `speechSynthesis.cancel()`

## Common Pitfalls
- ESM: all files use `import`/`export` — never use `require()`
- Electron IPC: renderer uses `window.buddy.*` (contextBridge) — never access `ipcRenderer` directly
- `app.getPath('userData')` on Windows = `%APPDATA%\desk-buddy` (different from project dir)
- Box3 scaling: always call `new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(root)` AFTER adding all children, BEFORE scaling
- Assistant window has its own preload (`preload-assistant.cjs`) — do NOT reuse `preload.js`
- Preloads MUST be `.cjs` (or `preload.js` works because Electron forces CJS for preloads) — with `"type":"module"` in package.json, rename new preloads to `.cjs` to avoid ESM parse errors
